      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the length of the diagonal connecting points A and B in a rectangular prism, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem. The diagonals in a rectangular prism are considered as edges of a rectangular box with a length, width, and height made up by the dimensions of the rectangular prism.\n\nThus, the length of each edge of the box is either\n10,\n20,\nor\n10.\n\nSince both,\n60,\nor\n10\nare included amongst the dimensions, in one of them,\n60,\nour diagonal length can be calculated by applying the Pythagorean Theorem. \n\nThus, \n25\n\ninches is the result.",
